<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1.  The above results have been reviewed by the audit committee and have been approved and taken on record  nby the Board of Directors at their respective meetings held on May 8, 2020.  n2.   The financial statements have been prepared in accordance with Ind AS notified under the Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) Rules, 2015 as amended.  n3.   Management has exercised necessary due diligence to ensure that the said comparative results provide a true and fair view of its affairs.  n4.  Information as required by Regulation 52(4) of Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations  nand Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 is as per Annexure “1” attached.  n5. Previous period’s/year’s figures have been regrouped / reclassified wherever necessary to correspond with  nthe current period’s/year’s classification /disclosure.  n6.  The figures for the quarter ended March 31, 2020 and March 31, 2019 are the balancing figures between the  naudited figures for the year ended March 31, 2020 and audited figures for the nine months ended December  n31, 2019 and the audited figures for the year ended March 31, 2019 and audited figures for the nine months  nended December 31, 2018 respectively.  n7.   In line with Hon’ble NCLT order dated June 04, 2019, SBI Business Process Management Services Pvt. Ltd  n(SBIBPMSL) has amalgamated with SBI Cards and Payment Services Limited from the appointed date April  n01, 2018.  n8.     During the year the Company was converted to Public Limited from Private Limited and Registrar of  nCompanies has issued fresh certificate of incorporation dated August 20, 2019 and consequently the name of  nthe Company changed from SBI Cards and Payment Services Private Limited to SBI Cards and Payment  nServices Limited.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        n9.  During the quarter ended March 31, 2020, the Company had come up with an Initial Public Offering (IPO) of  n137,149,314 Equity Shares of face value of Rs. 10 each comprising of a Fresh Issue of 6,622,516 Equity Shares  nand an Offer for Sale of 130,526,798 Equity Shares aggregating to Rs.1,034,078.82 lakhs (Selling  nShareholders Rs. 984,146.35 lakhs and Rs. 49,932.47 lakhs of the Company). The equity shares of the  nCompany were listed on Bombay Stock Exchange Limited and National Stock Exchange of India Limited on  nMarch 16, 2020.  n10.   Pursuant to Regulation 32 (1) there is no deviation/ variation in the utilization of proceeds as mentioned in the objects stated in the Prospectus dated March 6, 2020, in respect of the Initial Public Offering of the Company.   n11.   The Board of Directors have declared interim dividend of Re 1 per equity share (10%) of the face value of Rs 10 per equity share for the financial year 2019-20, after the close of the reporting year, in accordance with  nSection 123(3) of the Companies Act, 2013, as amended.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 n  n                                                                                             nNote:. Since there is a limit of words that can be entered in the Notes to accounts, therefore, for Information Pursuant to the Regulation 52(4) of Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, and  for other note of Accounts  please refer the results in PDF format filed by the Company.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
